Turn fast mode on and off from the web chat, and report whether it is on.

claude-native: /fast is no longer escaped into plain text. /fast on and
/fast off reach Claude Code as typed and show as a command in the chat; a bare
/fast becomes /fast on or /fast off from the last statusLine capture, since a
bare /fast may open a picker. The statusLine's fast_mode is kept in
context.json and posted as external_session_usage data.fast_mode whenever it
changes.

codex-native: /fast, /fast on and /fast off switch the thread to Codex's Fast
service tier (priority) or back with thread/settings/update, and record it as
service_tier in the session's config.toml, instead of starting a turn. The
forwarder posts data.fast_mode from thread start/resume and every
thread/settings/updated, so /fast typed in the terminal shows too.

Pairs with the server patch 0008-fast-mode.patch and the web patch
0009-composer-fast-mode.patch. Applies after 0001-rate-limits.patch. Base:
omnigent v0.15.0 (c8b9b85f822f).

